  "_comment": "Hand-verified Surah-boundary crop points for pages where a Surah's ornamental heading box shares a physical scanned page with the end of the previous Surah (see PDF-CONTENT.md §4a). Each entry is keyed 'fromSurah->toSurah' and gives the split line on that shared page, as splitPt = distance in PDF points from the TOP of the page down to the first safely-blank row immediately before the incoming Surah's heading-box top border. generate-surah-pdfs.mjs converts this to a PDF-space y (pageHeightPts - splitPt) and applies it as a CropBox: the outgoing Surah's copy of this page keeps only the region ABOVE the split (excludes the incoming Surah's heading box and everything after); the incoming Surah's copy keeps only the region AT/BELOW the split (excludes the outgoing Surah's tail ayahs). Determined by rendering each shared page (scripts/pdf/_explore-*.mjs, not part of the shipped app) and reading the true blank gap between the last ayah's ink and the heading box's own top border — never by formula, since these scans' internal page geometry doesn't follow a fixed grid (PDF-CONTENT.md §1).",
